    "text": "To determine the total time Tyson spent in his races, we need to calculate the time spent in each type of race and then sum these times.\n\nFirst, let's find out how many races Tyson had in each type of water. Since he had ten total races and half of them were in lakes and half were in the ocean, we have:\n\\[ \\text{Number of races in lakes} = \\frac{10}{2} = 5 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Number of races in the ocean} = \\frac{10}{2} = 5 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the time spent in each type of race. The time spent in a race is given by the formula:\n\\[ \\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}} \\]\n\nFor the races in the lake:\n\\[ \\text{Time in lake races} = \\frac{3 \\text{ miles}}{3 \\text{ mph}} = 1 \\text{ hour} \\]\nSince he had 5 races in the lake, the total time spent in lake races is:\n\\[ 5 \\times 1 \\text{ hour} = 5 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nFor the races in the ocean:\n\\[ \\text{Time in ocean races} = \\frac{3 \\text{ miles}}{2.5 \\text{ mph}} = \\frac{3}{2.5} = 1.2 \\text{ hours} \\]\nSince he had 5 races in the ocean, the total time spent in ocean races is:\n\\[ 5 \\times 1.2 \\text{ hours} = 6 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nFinally, we add the time spent in both types of races to get the total time spent in all races:\n\\[ 5 \\text{ hours} + 6 \\text{ hours} = 11 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nThus, the total time Tyson spent in his races is:\n\\[ \\boxed{11} \\]",
